      {
        "id": "sc_note_a",
        "type": "flograph.util.note",
        "pos": [
          560,
          1500
        ],
        "params": {
          "text": "## A \u00b7 Controls that drive a chart's settings\n\nEach control publishes a variable (*Behaviour \u25b8 Variable name*). The chart's **Kind**, **Group and total** and **Log Y** settings are *bound* to them \u2014 right-click a setting in Properties \u25b8 **Use Variable** \u2014 and its title says `Revenue \u2014 ${how} by month`.\n\nThese three are set to apply **instantly**, so the chart follows each click. It draws the rows the form in **B** keeps.",
          "width": 560,
          "height": 0
        },
        "code": null,
        "label": null,
        "description": "",
        "active": true,
        "locked": false,
        "frozen": false,
        "manual": false,
        "frozen_fingerprint": null,
        "exclusive": null,
        "preview": true,
        "port_labels": null,
        "flow_pins": null,
        "ports_collapsed": false,
        "color": null,
        "compact_view": null,
        "mark": "",
        "mark_text": "",
        "mark_image": "",
        "z": 14,
        "extra_inputs": []
      },
      {
        "id": "sc_readout",
        "type": "flograph.scripting.python_script",
        "pos": [
          2220,
          300
        ],
        "params": {},
        "code": "\"\"\"What each control sends\n\nA readout: every control in this frame is wired into one of these inputs,\nand the table shows exactly the value that reaches the flow \u2014 type and all.\n\"\"\"\nNODE = {\n    \"label\": \"What each control sends\",\n    \"category\": \"Scripting\",\n    \"version\": \"1.0\",\n    \"inputs\": [(name, \"any\", {\"optional\": True}) for name in (\n        \"number\", \"text\", \"date\", \"time\", \"moment\", \"low\", \"high\",\n        \"colour\", \"file\", \"ticked\", \"multi\")],\n    \"outputs\": [(\"table\", \"dataframe\")],\n}\n\n\ndef run(ctx, **inputs):\n    import pandas as pd\n    rows = [{\"input\": name, \"value\": repr(value),\n             \"type\": type(value).__name__}\n            for name, value in inputs.items() if value is not None]\n    return {\"table\": pd.DataFrame(rows, columns=[\"input\", \"value\", \"type\"])}\n",
        "label": "What each control sends",
        "description": "",
        "active": true,
        "locked": false,
        "frozen": false,
        "manual": false,
        "frozen_fingerprint": null,
        "exclusive": null,
        "preview": true,
        "port_labels": null,
        "flow_pins": null,
        "ports_collapsed": false,
        "color": null,
        "compact_view": null,
        "mark": "",
        "mark_text": "",
        "mark_image": "",
        "z": 15,
        "extra_inputs": []
      },
